course: dictionary
lesson: 14502
title: Peekaboo
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peekaboo can be a noun or an interjection, and context shows you which one. «Baby Mia giggled every time Dad played peekaboo with her.» Here peekaboo is a game, because Dad plays it with her.
explain: «Grandma hid behind the door, then jumped out and cried, "Peekaboo!"» Here peekaboo is a word you shout when you show your face again. The surprise and the jump tell you it is a playful moment.
explain: Peekaboo can also describe clothes. «The lace top was peekaboo, with a small gap at the shoulder.» The words around it tell you that peekaboo means the gap lets something show. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: Peekaboo is a game where you hide your face and then show it again.
fact: «Peekaboo!» is what you say when you show your face in that game.
fact: Babies and toddlers often love peekaboo, and it helps them learn that things still exist when they are hidden.
fact: A peekaboo top or dress has a small gap or hole that lets something show through.
fact: Peekaboo can be a noun (the game) or an interjection (a word you shout).
exercise: «Baby Mia giggled when Dad played peekaboo with her.» What is peekaboo in this sentence? | A type of bed | A loud noise like a drum | A kind of food for babies | *A game where you hide your face and then show it
exercise: «She covered her eyes, then said, "Peekaboo!"» Why does she say peekaboo? | To ask for a drink | To say goodbye for ever | To tell everyone to be quiet | *To show her face again in a playful way
exercise: «The lace top was peekaboo, with a small gap at the shoulder.» What does peekaboo mean here? | Covered in paint | Very heavy and warm | Brand new and shiny | *Having a small gap or hole that lets something show
test: «Grandma hid behind the door and jumped out, saying, "Peekaboo!"» What does the word show? | *A surprise and a playful moment | A word for a sleeping cat | A sign that it is bedtime | A cross, angry shout
test: Which sentence uses peekaboo to mean a game? | «The peekaboo bus was late again.» | «He drank a peekaboo of cold juice.» | «The peekaboo dog barked at the postman.» | *«We played peekaboo until the baby laughed.»
exam: Ben asks, «What does peekaboo mean?» Which answer is best? | A loud shout for help | A type of sandwich with jam | *A game where you hide your face and then show it | A kind of fish that lives in rivers
